# Build context exclusions (P3-007).
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile would bake the following into the
# production image: the developer's virtualenv (hundreds of MB), the local
# SQLite database, generated evidence (data/raw = tool stdout, exports), the
# VCS history, and -- most importantly -- the local .env, i.e. real secrets.
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# secrets
docker/.env
*.pem
*.key

# Keep the example so operators can see which vars to set. The negation MUST
# come last: dockerignore is last-match-wins, so a broad `.env*` rule placed
# after this line would silently re-include the real secret.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# local data / generated artifacts
data/
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
*.log
/media/
/staticfiles/

# VCS and docs that do not belong in a runtime image
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
docs/
tests/
*.md
!README.md
